# Workshop NCB (Eurosystem) root certificate.
#
# This file is the trust anchor the wallet uses to verify offline DE
# tokens (`de-offline+jwt`) per ADR 0010 §1. Like every other workshop
# trust root in this fork (cf. resources-logic/src/main/res/raw/
# accesa_workshop_ca.pem) it is replaced verbatim from the companion
# repo when the backend lands or rotates:
#
#   companion-repo/services/ncb-issuer/src/main/resources/workshop-root/cert.pem
#
# Until that file is populated, the wallet will reject every minted
# token at storeTokens() with TOKEN_SIGNATURE_INVALID. That is the
# correct fail-closed behaviour — a wallet with no trust anchor must
# not store bearer claims it cannot verify.
#
# When the M4a backend agent generates the workshop NCB root, copy its
# `cert.pem` content over THIS WHOLE FILE (leading comments included
# can stay; PEM parsing ignores them).
